{"name":"Movie Magic","hex":"#b2bfd5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"movie","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A recorded sequence of images displayed on a screen at a rate sufficiently fast to create the appearance of motion; a film; a video.","A professionally made motion picture of a substantive narrative work, typically around 1 to 3 hours long, typically intended for cinema, art, entertainment, and a widespread audience; a feature film, theatrical film."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/movie"},{"term":"magic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The application of rituals or actions, especially those based on occult knowledge, to subdue or manipulate natural or supernatural beings and forces in order to have some benefit from them. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","The supernatural forces which are drawn on in such a ritual."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having supernatural talents, properties or qualities attributed to magic.","Producing extraordinary results, as though through the use of magic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/magic"}],"entries":[{"title":"Movie Magic Special Effects Show","blocks":[{"text":"Movie Magic Special Effects Show was a live show at the Warner Bros. Movie World amusement park at Oxenford, Gold Coast, Queensland, Australia. The show opened with the park in 1991 as part of a larger studio tour. The studio tour closed first followed by the show in 2005. The Superman Escape station building was the former home to the Movie Magic Special Effects Show."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Movie_Magic_Special_Effects_Show","wikidata":"Q6926850"},{"title":"Movie Magic Screenwriter","blocks":[{"text":"Movie Magic Screenwriter is a word processing program sold by Write Brothers to format screenplays, teleplays and novels."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/aa/MovieMagicScreenwriter.jpg/330px-MovieMagicScreenwriter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Movie_Magic_Screenwriter","wikidata":"Q16974369"},{"title":"Magic (1978 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Magic is a 1978 American psychological horror drama film directed by Richard Attenborough and starring Anthony Hopkins, Ann-Margret and Burgess Meredith. The screenplay is by William Goldman, who adapted his novel of the same title. The score was composed by Jerry Goldsmith."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/91/Magicposter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magic_(1978_film)","wikidata":"Q910887"},{"title":"Film","blocks":[{"text":"A film, movie, or motion picture is a work of visual art that simulates experiences and otherwise communicates ideas, stories, perceptions, emotions, or atmosphere through the use of moving images that are generally, since the 1930s, synchronized with sound and sometimes feature other sensory stimuli."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Le_Voyage_dans_la_Lune_%281902%29.webm/330px--Le_Voyage_dans_la_Lune_%281902%29.webm.jpg","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Film","wikidata":"Q11424"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Prof._Stampfer%27s_Stroboscopische_Scheibe_No._X.gif/500px-Prof._Stampfer%27s_Stroboscopische_Scheibe_No._X.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Prof._Stampfer%27s_Stroboscopische_Scheibe_No._X.gif/500px-Prof._Stampfer%27s_Stroboscopische_Scheibe_No._X.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Animated GIF of Prof. Stampfer's Stroboscopische Scheibe No. X (Trentsensky & Vieweg 1833)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AProf._Stampfer's_Stroboscopische_Scheibe_No._X.gif"},{"srcset"